---
import AppFrame from "@/components/AppFrame.astro";
import BaseLayout from "@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

// The Swedish page is /pensionskalkylator. The calculator is the same file, started in English.
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Pension savings calculator – your future pension capital"
  description="Work out your future pension capital from your saving, return and fees, and see what it gives per month."
  ogTitle="Pension savings calculator – Pensionslyft"
  ogDescription="See your future pension capital and monthly amount after fees."
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 pt-10 pb-14">
    <h1 class="sr-only">Pension savings calculator</h1>
    <AppFrame slug="pensionssparande" title="Pension savings calculator" />

    <section class="mt-12 border-t border-border pt-10">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold">What does the pension savings calculator cover?</h2>
      <div class="mt-4 max-w-3xl space-y-3 text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground">
        <p>
          The calculator is for private pension, IPS (individual pension saving), occupational pension and private
          saving, but not the public pension. Note that pension is normally taxed as income when it is paid out, which
          private saving is not, because the tax on it has already been paid.
        </p>
        <p>
          Within private saving it also matters how the capital is taxed. For an ISK (investment savings account), a
          capital insurance and a securities insurance you pay a yield tax every year. For a securities account, a fund
          account and a custody account you pay capital gains tax only when you sell, if there has been a gain.
        </p>
        <p>
          The public pension is always paid for life. To include the public pension as well, see the
          <a href="/en/calculators" class="text-primary underline underline-offset-2">other calculators</a>
          (in Swedish for now).
        </p>
        <p>
          The calculation is an estimate before tax and not individual advice. The return is not guaranteed.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
